## Post-implementation step-by-step AC testing

After implementation, automatically create a tester-facing guide for delivery work with manually testable ACs; also trigger when the user asks for a "UT doc", "UAT doc", "test evidence", "QA walkthrough", or "screenshot proof". If no AC can be tested manually, record `n/a` in the change doc instead of manufacturing a guide.

Copy [`docs/_templates/_TEMPLATE_step-by-step-test.md`](../../docs/_templates/_TEMPLATE_step-by-step-test.md) to `docs/ut/<work-id>/<slug>-<alias-slug>-step-by-step-test.md`, with `assets/<alias-slug>/` and an optional PDF. Keep one `#` title, one intro line linking back to `changes/<slug>.md#acceptance-criteria-visual-delta`, and one `##` per AC/scenario.

**Environment selection:**

1. Resolve `<test-org-alias>` from the user-supplied alias or the project default; record the alias and Org ID in the guide.
2. A user may supply an additional/higher-environment alias. Create a separate alias-qualified guide/evidence set for it, rediscover records there, and never transplant IDs from another org.
3. Treat an added environment as read-only until the user authorizes exact create/update/delete/external actions, record scope, side effects, cleanup, approver, and timestamp.
4. Run the real process only after any applicable Gate B has passed; never use an underlying helper as a substitute.

**Prepare the unchecked guide:**

1. FIND a real eligible record (prefer real over synthetic). If none qualifies, MODIFY one or FORCE the gap for a negative case.
2. Snapshot every staged value for rollback. Add negative, bulk, concurrency, permission, and regression scenarios required by accepted Gate findings.
3. Add a test-record ledger and exact input ledger. Provide distinctive, non-sensitive values (work ID + scenario ID + UTC marker) so later queries can prove which records the run created.
4. For every screen/form, list the exact UI path, field label, value to enter/select, button, expected immediate result, and stop condition.
5. For every created record, provide at least one deterministic discovery method: (a) a stable parent/marker/time-window query or (b) an exact UI path such as **Parent → Related → related list → newest matching marker**. Include both when available. Never leave “record ID: ____” without a way to find it, and never rely only on newest-record ordering.
6. Capture real before and current screenshots with concrete environment/record/value captions under `assets/<alias-slug>/`. Names are `<scenario-anchor>-before-<what>.png` and `<scenario-anchor>-after-<what>.png`. If a real before run is unavailable, replace its image with `source-backed baseline only`; never fake a screenshot.
7. Give every scenario explicit stable anchors (`<scenario-anchor>-test` in the guide and `<scenario-anchor>-visual-delta` in the change doc). State **Earlier behavior** and **Current behavior**, and link directly both ways.
8. Verify eligibility and blast radius before execution, run the shipped process, query the outcome, restore staged source values, and leave process-created evidence records in place unless the user approves cleanup.

**Tester → agent completion loop:**

1. Hand the unchecked guide to the tester and wait. The tester checks steps, enters actual values/IDs/errors, then says verification is done.
2. On that message, read every tester entry and independently repeat the recorded read-only query and/or exact UI discovery method against the guide's declared alias.
3. Verify parentage, time window, marker, RecordType/type, exact values, counts, relationships, negative assertions, and absence of hidden/duplicate records.
4. Fill blanks the recorded discovery method proves and correct stale/mistyped entries with query/UI evidence. A tester checkmark is not agent evidence: leave anything unproved unchecked and explain the blocker.
5. Do not rerun or mutate the process merely to complete the document; ask first if verification needs a new execution.

Virtualized/iframed lists often cannot be text-searched — scroll the container until the target row renders, then screenshot the real row.

**Commit only when asked, explicit paths:** initial commit = guide + staging/rollback artifacts + screenshots + optional PDF; second commit = living change-doc link/hash backfill. After the tester says done, commit the verified guide, then separately backfill the living change doc with that verified-results hash.

