## Anti-patterns (all touchpoints)

- Starting code without a confirmed ticket — extract the number from the message/screenshot, or ASK if it's missing (never guess) — or forgetting to rename the chat to `<ticket> - <description>` after confirming, or treating a screenshot as the source of truth instead of transcribing it.
- Letting "see attached screenshot" land in §3.
- Skipping the pre-coding analysis / writing the LLD AFTER coding as a rationalization. The LLD is a design tool — author it before code.
- Skipping a gate that applies, or gating work the review rule exempts; launching fewer than the two defect critics plus the minimality critic; running them serially when parallel launch is available; coaching them toward approval; substituting an unlabeled self-review; majority-voting away a blocker; or proceeding on stale verdicts after a material plan/diff change.
- Re-running or informally reproducing a gate the user waived.
- Producing the questions-and-kt or walkthrough doc by reflex when there are no open questions; duplicating the full design into both the LLD and the change doc.
- Diagrams whose subgraphs are logical phases instead of named components, a missing legend, colour as the only signal, or node IDs renamed between the current and proposed diagrams.
- Inlining the doc into the code commit, or skipping the doc "because the commit message says it all" (it has no rollback/verification/follow-ups).
- `git add force-app/` (blanket-add) when another agent may be active; including someone else's file because it was "already modified".
- Missing the `**Manifest:**` line for a `--manifest` deploy; skipping Diff-highlights for OmniScripts/IPs/DRs/layouts; pasting a 500-line file into a diff fence.
- UT/UAT: synthetic data when a real record exists; modifying real records without snapshot+rollback; calling the underlying function instead of the shipped process; reusing IDs across orgs; unspecified form inputs; a created-record blank with no discovery query/UI path; trusting tester checkmarks without read-only verification; inventing a before screenshot; or a report screenshot that doesn't actually show the target row.

## Adapting to other projects

Stack-agnostic. Map terms to your stack: process under test → batch/job/endpoint; record → entity/row; component/engine → class/module/service; downstream automation → triggers/jobs/events; read-only query → DB/API read. Keep `changes/`, `docs/lld/`, `docs/ut/` at the repo root (or adjust paths consistently here and in the templates). Sandbox alias is `{{ORG_ALIAS}}` in this repo; set per-project from `sf config get target-org`.
